  "application_type": "Prior Approval",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal fails to comply with the terms of Article 4 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 an amended because: the enlarged part of the dwelling house would connect to an existing two storey rear extension and as a result would be contrary to Schedule Part 1 Class A A.1 (ja) of the GPDO (2015) as the enlarged part of the dwellinghouse would have more than one storey and extend beyond the rear wall of the original dwellinghouse by more than 3 metres.\r\nFurther, during the site visit it was noted that all the doors were fire doors with separate locks, there was a shared kitchen and fire exit signs. It is therefore reasonable to doubt that the use of this house is as a single-family dwelling. As a result, the application property is not eligible under schedule 2 Class A of the GPDO (2015).\r\n"
